WEBVTT

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:05.310
Hello again, Keiko-san.

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:09.690
You already know it's about time, right?

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:14.900
You wanna head back to the past, don't you?

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:15.480
Yes.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:20.900
Are you <i>really</i> sure, though?

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:29.840
I mean, you're about as happy as most 
people could hope to be this world.

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:35.750
You've got a wife, a little girl, 
a job where they rely on you...

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:40.850
I honestly don't see why you'd 
wanna head back to those hard times.

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:46.700
You're really willing to throw 
this happiness aside

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:51.030
to head back to the past, young man?

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:47.710
I guess that's my answer.

00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:49.140
I...

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:55.510
I didn't go back in time 
because I wanted to be happy.

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:59.000
It wasn't about getting a nice girl...

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:04.130
Or using cheats to become a hero.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:08.700
I wanted to struggle. To be hurt.

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:11.970
To lose hope... To be pushed to the edge.

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:13.800
And with them...

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:17.210
If I can go through it all with them...

00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:22.800
I'd take that over a happy future any day.

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:26.780
I want to go back.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:32.180
I want to go back to the past, 
to be with everyone.

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:34.900
Back when we were all together...

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:37.090
I want to go back!

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:38.480
Here.

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:49.250
You've got a good look to you right now.

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:55.580
Okay, let's do this thing.

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:01.320
Wait a second!

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:05.470
What now? Having second thoughts after all?

00:04:05.770 --> 00:04:10.240
Over the last few months, 
I've met a lot of different people.

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:13.450
I have thoughts about them all, but...

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:16.330
No regrets.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:17.690
Still...

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:23.490
There's someone I have to say goodbye to.

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:30.790
I getcha. Go on, then.

00:04:49.170 --> 00:04:50.180
I'm home!

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:52.340
Hey, hey, Daddy!

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:53.780
What is it?

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:57.890
Y'know what? I found out that 
Mommy is really good at drawing!

00:04:57.890 --> 00:04:59.560
She is?

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:02.030
Yeah! Look at this!

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:03.990
This is...

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:08.190
It's Shinoaki's art.

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:12.690
Honey, welcome home...

00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:16.250
Maki! Did you already show him?

00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:19.130
What happened? With the art.

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:22.120
Well...

00:05:23.270 --> 00:05:27.050
I tried that game you told me about.

00:05:27.770 --> 00:05:29.600
You mean MysClo?

00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:32.110
Minori Ayaka-san...

00:05:32.110 --> 00:05:36.500
I thought her art was really wonderful.

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:39.270
It made me want to... try drawing.

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:42.430
One other thing...

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:46.430
You blame yourself for everybody quitting,

00:05:46.430 --> 00:05:49.590
but you managed to help 
one person, at least.

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:50.450
I did?

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:52.030
I mean Minori Ayaka.

00:05:58.930 --> 00:06:01.590
Uh... Kyoya-kun?

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:04.390
Daddy? What's wrong?

00:06:04.390 --> 00:06:06.100
Hey, Daddy?

00:06:32.920 --> 00:06:34.620
It's real strange.

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:37.960
I hadn't drawn in so long...

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:43.750
But soon as I got the itch, 
it happened real naturally.

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:48.110
It only took the littlest thing.

00:06:48.710 --> 00:06:50.130
I'm sorry.

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:52.720
It ain't anything for you to apologize for.

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:54.870
I couldn't draw anymore...

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:59.900
But I had you, and I had Maki.

00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:03.150
That made me think it'd be okay.

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:07.060
The next day would always come...

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:10.120
And I thought that was good enough.

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:15.090
But y'know... when 
I started wanting to draw...

00:07:15.730 --> 00:07:19.350
A bunch of stuff I had 
forgotten hit me real hard...

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:23.020
It was a lot of fun.

00:07:23.370 --> 00:07:24.960
So much...

00:07:30.150 --> 00:07:31.880
So, Kyoya-kun...

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:39.810
Y'know, I... wanna make 
a bunch of art again.

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:46.060
So... when I'm working, 
I'm gonna be kinda...

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:49.000
Focused, y'know?

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:51.580
And as far as Maki goes, I dunno if—

00:07:52.220 --> 00:07:53.810
Don't worry.

00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:58.650
I'll support you however I can.

00:07:58.650 --> 00:08:03.180
So, it's okay for you to work on your art.

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:07.960
Thank you, Kyoya-kun.

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:09.960
Yeah.

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:14.850
Y'know, I wanna try drawing something big!

00:08:15.190 --> 00:08:19.150
I'm not sure how it's
 gonna turn out at first,

00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:21.980
so I'll go small on backgrounds...

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:25.950
But then, I wanna draw 
something a lot bigger...

00:08:25.950 --> 00:08:28.230
A place with lots of space!

00:08:28.810 --> 00:08:32.850
It can be in nature, or in the city...

00:08:32.850 --> 00:08:34.670
And girls!

00:08:35.260 --> 00:08:40.870
I dunno what kinda girls folks 
are drawing these days.

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:45.660
I can't wait to see what people are doing.

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:49.500
And then, y'know what else?

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:27.170
Okay, I'm heading out.

00:09:27.430 --> 00:09:29.870
Okay. Be careful.

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:31.840
Daddy, have a good day!

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:41.850
Daddy, too tight!

00:09:43.940 --> 00:09:45.300
Thank you.

00:09:51.930 --> 00:09:53.250
Thank you.

00:09:57.610 --> 00:09:58.660
Off I go.

00:09:59.090 --> 00:10:00.430
Have a good day!

00:10:00.430 --> 00:10:01.910
Have a good day!

00:10:22.860 --> 00:10:24.460
Looks like you're done.

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:30.210
There's something I wanna tell you.

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:32.810
What's that?

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:36.450
You've been talking about this 
power of yours in a bad way,

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:39.810
like it's a cheat, or you're playing dirty.

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:46.120
"I know the future, so it's only 
natural that I can pull stuff off."

00:10:46.920 --> 00:10:50.370
But you've never played dirty.

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:54.210
You haven't used your knowledge 
to hurt other people,

00:10:54.210 --> 00:10:56.790
and you haven't tried 
to unfairly profit off of it, either.

00:10:58.130 --> 00:11:00.450
You've only been using your own strength,

00:11:00.450 --> 00:11:02.900
and you've always considered 
other people before acting.

00:11:02.900 --> 00:11:05.980
That's how you were able to 
gain their trust, y'know?

00:11:06.530 --> 00:11:09.640
You think people trust me?

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:11.060
Yeah, man.

00:11:11.570 --> 00:11:16.540
That's why Kawasegawa-chan and 
Shinoaki-chan were both so grateful to you.

00:11:16.540 --> 00:11:20.920
I'd bet that goes for Nanako-chan 
and Tsurayuki-kun, too.

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:25.130
I hope you're right.

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:29.960
Anyway, that said, 
it ain't like you're a hero.

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:32.370
You're still a interloper 
who's popped in from outta nowhere

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:36.260
and changing the future 
from what it originally was.

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:39.630
Doing it for their sake, 
or trying to help 'em...

00:11:40.330 --> 00:11:44.080
You get that's not how 
this works now, right?

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:45.350
Yeah.

00:11:45.920 --> 00:11:50.230
I think now that I was really full of myself.

00:11:51.160 --> 00:11:53.870
I thought by using this 
power to help people...

00:11:53.870 --> 00:11:57.230
I could be like their savior.

00:11:57.560 --> 00:12:01.290
But that was just my ego talking.

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:06.710
So I'm done trying to act high and mighty.

00:12:06.710 --> 00:12:11.520
I'm going to trust the others, 
believe in myself...

00:12:11.520 --> 00:12:13.090
and give it my all.

00:12:16.570 --> 00:12:18.670
Well, welcome back, protagonist!

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:20.670
Hope you're ready for hell again!

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:26.050
Let's get a move on, then.

00:12:40.250 --> 00:12:41.520
Kyoya!

00:12:41.960 --> 00:12:44.880
Shinoaki! Kyoya's awake!

00:12:44.880 --> 00:12:46.470
Kyoya, are you okay?

00:12:46.470 --> 00:12:48.990
You collapsed out front! 
We were really worried!

00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:52.960
Nanako... I'm home.

00:12:53.810 --> 00:12:55.820
Uh... welcome home.

00:12:55.820 --> 00:12:58.400
Kyoya-kun! You're awake!

00:12:58.820 --> 00:13:00.000
Shinoaki...

00:13:02.810 --> 00:13:05.310
Anyway, Kyoya, there's bad news!

00:13:05.310 --> 00:13:07.300
Tsurayuki's dropping out of school.

00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:10.780
He said he told you already.

00:13:10.780 --> 00:13:13.400
Then he came here to say good-bye 
to Shinoaki and me.

00:13:13.400 --> 00:13:16.850
What in tarnation happened 
with him, Kyoya-kun?

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:20.930
I see. Okay.

00:13:20.930 --> 00:13:23.150
For now... let's consider the future.

00:13:24.090 --> 00:13:25.820
What do you mean?

00:13:26.590 --> 00:13:30.240
I'm going to step outside 
for a sec. I won't be long.

00:13:31.610 --> 00:13:32.830
Kyoya-kun!

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:36.250
Kyoya-kun... you're coming back, right?

00:13:37.950 --> 00:13:42.500
It's okay. I'm not going anywhere anymore.

00:14:05.290 --> 00:14:06.730
<i>This is where I'll start.</i>

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:10.660
<i>No more regrets.</i>

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:13.420
<i>It's not that I think I'm always right...</i>

00:14:13.420 --> 00:14:16.350
<i>I'm not a champion of justice, 
or some kind of hero.</i>

00:14:16.760 --> 00:14:20.830
<i>I'm just going to chase 
the things I believe in.</i>

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:23.630
<i>I want to make something.</i>

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:26.340
<i>I went ten years back in time 
because I wanted to create.</i>

00:14:27.150 --> 00:14:30.580
<i>I didn't bring some kind 
of cheating advantage to the past...</i>

00:14:31.540 --> 00:14:34.100
<i>Just the kind of passion 
that I'll never have again.</i>

00:14:42.330 --> 00:14:47.440
<i>This is when our remake really starts.</i>

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:53.450
<b>Oonaka University of the Arts</b>

00:15:07.810 --> 00:15:09.400
What's up, Hashiba?!

00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:10.960
You're looking kinda down!

00:15:10.960 --> 00:15:12.220
Summer heat getting to you?

00:15:12.580 --> 00:15:15.660
Nah, I'm fine. Nothing to worry about.

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:17.610
That so?

00:15:17.610 --> 00:15:20.190
Well, if you ever feel 
worn out, just holler!

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:22.800
I know some bishoujo games 
 that'll have you wondering

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:26.250
how you could've ever been feeling down!

00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:32.610
Momotaro-san, Momotaro-san!

00:15:32.610 --> 00:15:36.770
The dumplings on your waist,

00:15:33.220 --> 00:15:35.240
Peaches!

00:15:36.050 --> 00:15:38.540
Oh, watch me spin like a peach!

00:15:36.770 --> 00:15:42.750
might I trouble you for one?

00:15:40.840 --> 00:15:42.750
Y'know, Hashy...

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:44.630
You're looking a lot older all of a sudden.

00:15:45.060 --> 00:15:46.880
I hadn't noticed.

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:49.610
I know! And I know how you feel, but...

00:15:49.610 --> 00:15:54.630
This is the kinda thing that other 
people have to point out to you.

00:15:54.630 --> 00:15:55.800
Wouldn't you say, Hiyama-chan?

00:15:55.800 --> 00:15:57.340
I think so.

00:15:57.340 --> 00:15:59.760
Although you're looking 
pretty rough around the edges

00:15:59.760 --> 00:16:01.230
after these last two months, too.

00:16:01.950 --> 00:16:05.770
<i>Things have gotten back to normal so 
completely that it's easy to wonder</i>

00:16:06.510 --> 00:16:09.150
<i>if that time in the future ever happened.</i>

00:16:09.650 --> 00:16:12.150
<i>Everyone seems to be the same.</i>

00:16:12.810 --> 00:16:14.740
<i>But Tsurayuki is still gone.</i>

00:16:16.030 --> 00:16:19.160
Rokuonji said that it was family business.

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:22.330
Have you heard any specifics, Hashiba?

00:16:24.220 --> 00:16:27.630
No. Nothing in particular.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:31.140
I see.

00:16:35.400 --> 00:16:39.900
It's a shame, considering his 
tuition woes were finally solved.

00:16:40.260 --> 00:16:41.270
Yeah.

00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:45.340
<i>He hasn't come back to school.</i>

00:16:45.830 --> 00:16:48.110
<i>But I'm not giving up.</i>

00:16:49.140 --> 00:16:54.110
<i>If he's Kawagoe Kyoichi, 
I know we'll meet again.</i>

00:16:55.610 --> 00:17:00.350
<i>And I've noticed signs of change 
with Nanako and Shinoaki.</i>

00:17:00.980 --> 00:17:02.190
Kyoya...

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:05.160
About the thing I mentioned the other day...

00:17:05.160 --> 00:17:07.530
What do you think?

00:17:07.530 --> 00:17:11.230
You mean the romantic messages 
you got from a fan?

00:17:11.230 --> 00:17:13.550
Not that!

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:16.090
The one about the offer.

00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:21.610
A circle that's making a dojin game 
asked me to work with them.

00:17:21.940 --> 00:17:25.100
Oh, for composing and
 performing their theme song?

00:17:26.050 --> 00:17:27.690
Why not give it a try?

00:17:28.630 --> 00:17:31.930
But y'know... it's kinda scary.

00:17:32.710 --> 00:17:35.700
Working with people who I don't know.

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:37.440
Why not just jump in and give it a try?

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:41.780
Like when you started uploading
 your songs, remember?

00:17:41.780 --> 00:17:45.330
You were the one who handled that, though.

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:51.730
Right? So... could you maybe...

00:17:54.100 --> 00:17:56.970
Nanako, try and do it on your own, okay?

00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:01.610
Kyoya, you're so mean!

00:18:01.610 --> 00:18:05.020
<i>Nanako was on the verge 
of becoming dependent on me.</i>

00:18:01.610 --> 00:18:07.490
What's the big deal?! 
It wouldn't kill you to help!

00:18:05.980 --> 00:18:08.170
<i>I'm not sure how much it'll help,</i>

00:18:08.170 --> 00:18:11.520
<i>but I'm going to try and 
prioritize her independence.</i>

00:18:12.760 --> 00:18:17.230
<i>And hopefully, one day, I'll meet N@NA.</i>

00:18:19.500 --> 00:18:21.100
<i>As for Shinoaki...</i>

00:18:21.640 --> 00:18:25.560
Just don't feel like drawing.

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:28.960
<b><i>Sukiyamon</i></b>

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:28.960
<b>Soy Sauce Flavor</b>

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:30.030
<i>Things were even more severe.</i>

00:18:32.450 --> 00:18:33.870
Soy sauce?

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:37.970
<i>Maybe it's burnout from 
having just finished a game.</i>

00:18:38.570 --> 00:18:42.470
<i>Or maybe a side effect from 
having compromised so much.</i>

00:18:43.320 --> 00:18:46.820
<i>Shinoaki, who used to 
be so excited about art,</i>

00:18:46.820 --> 00:18:49.110
<i>is keeping her distance from it now.</i>

00:18:53.730 --> 00:18:58.320
There's just... nothing 
I want to draw anymore.

00:18:58.640 --> 00:19:01.880
<i>I need to help her find 
a way through this.</i>

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:06.240
<i>But what would work?</i>

00:19:40.500 --> 00:19:41.730
Ow, ow...

00:19:41.730 --> 00:19:43.000
Yow...

00:19:43.460 --> 00:19:45.810
S-Sorry! Were you hurt?

00:19:46.810 --> 00:19:50.850
S-S-Sorry! Sorry! I'm okay!

00:19:52.020 --> 00:19:54.050
Let me help you.

00:20:01.980 --> 00:20:03.280
<i>Wow.</i>

00:20:10.920 --> 00:20:11.850
Was that...

00:20:11.850 --> 00:20:13.850
I-It's nothing! Really.

00:20:14.290 --> 00:20:17.060
<i>Why does she have a copy of the game?</i>

00:20:17.530 --> 00:20:20.280
<i>Maybe she's into that sort of thing.</i>

00:20:23.360 --> 00:20:25.410
<b>Saikawa            Minori</b>

00:20:30.820 --> 00:20:33.640
Um, s-s-sorry!

00:20:33.640 --> 00:20:36.010
I-I'm really sorry about running into you!

00:20:36.010 --> 00:20:38.770
But I'm going to be late 
for class, so excuse me!

00:20:44.450 --> 00:20:47.860
I see. So that's how it is.

00:20:48.810 --> 00:20:52.000
<i>Everything has some purpose.</i>

00:20:53.300 --> 00:20:56.480
<i>You were right about that, Kawasegawa.</i>

00:20:57.950 --> 00:20:58.860
Okay!

00:21:12.400 --> 00:21:13.830
<i>I started taking action.</i>

00:21:18.440 --> 00:21:20.610
<i>I'll create an opportunity for Shinoaki,</i>

00:21:22.850 --> 00:21:26.240
<i>and give the future Minori Ayaka some hope.</i>

00:21:27.540 --> 00:21:32.640
<i>Granted, there's no guarantee 
that it'll work out for the best.</i>

00:21:30.640 --> 00:21:32.640
<b>Second-years will create a five-minute video project over two semesters.</b>

00:21:30.640 --> 00:21:32.640
<b>• Upload to Nico Nico Douga
• Submit the video file and URL where it was uploaded</b>

00:21:30.640 --> 00:21:32.640
<b>• Prizes will be awarded for the number of views, comments and favorites posted videos receive
over the first semester, second semester, and after one year.</b>

00:21:30.640 --> 00:21:32.640
<b>Cash prizes!</b>

00:21:33.160 --> 00:21:35.810
<i>It might not make any difference,</i>

00:21:35.810 --> 00:21:38.140
<i>and it could even make things worse.</i>

00:21:39.320 --> 00:21:42.480
<i>But... I have plenty of motivation,</i>

00:21:43.320 --> 00:21:46.520
<i>and the strong feelings I realized 
after traveling into the future.</i>

00:21:47.340 --> 00:21:49.180
<i>As long as I have that...</i>

00:21:49.180 --> 00:21:51.860
<i>I'm betting I'll have 
the confidence to take action.</i>

00:21:52.570 --> 00:21:55.420
<i>There used to be a group 
of people I looked up to.</i>

00:21:57.010 --> 00:22:01.060
<i>I thought they would 
always be out of reach.</i>

00:22:01.060 --> 00:22:04.060
<i>Now, they're right by my side.</i>

00:22:04.580 --> 00:22:09.570
<i>But in order for us to become 
the kind of people I used to idolize...</i>

00:22:18.140 --> 00:22:21.360
<b>To make the best project possible together</b>

00:22:22.340 --> 00:22:26.130
<i>This remake has only just begun.</i>

00:22:31.860 --> 00:22:35.450
Say, Kawasegawa... 
I wanted to ask you something.

00:22:35.880 --> 00:22:36.950
What is it?

00:22:36.950 --> 00:22:43.220
Let's say that I was in a lot of trouble, 
and asked you for help.

00:22:43.570 --> 00:22:46.710
Would you be willing to put 
everything else aside and help me?

00:22:50.980 --> 00:22:55.270
Hashiba, I think you 
need your head examined.

00:22:55.270 --> 00:22:58.960
R-Right. Sorry.

00:23:00.020 --> 00:23:02.430
But if you really needed the help...

00:23:03.630 --> 00:23:06.440
Then I guess I'd be willing to offer it.

